WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.926
Morning, Ziad.

00:00:00.926 --> 00:00:02.314
Wednesday the fourth.

00:00:02.314 --> 00:00:07.338
A warm one, a full workday, and a couple of things on there for the evening.

00:00:07.338 --> 00:00:09.784
Here's one to chew on while you move.

00:00:09.784 --> 00:00:15.668
When a podcast app checks the feed and nothing's changed, what does the server send back?

00:00:15.668 --> 00:00:16.990
Answer's at the end.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.511
Weather's a gift today.

00:00:18.511 --> 00:00:22.015
Sunny, up near seventy-two, with only a light breeze.

00:00:22.015 --> 00:00:30.939
Showers are possible tomorrow morning, and Friday looks like a real soaker, an inch or two of rain, so that's the day to skip the bike.

00:00:30.939 --> 00:00:31.865
Okay, the day.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.840
Calendar has the gym at seven, straight sets.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:41.715
There's a lens return on there too, sometime between eight and noon, and the exact time still isn't set.

00:00:41.715 --> 00:00:43.566
Then Godinger, nine to five.

00:00:43.566 --> 00:00:46.145
There's a call on there at five-thirty.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:50.243
And after that, a Breaking Bad night on the calendar at eight.

00:00:50.243 --> 00:00:53.747
So there's a little gap in the middle to grab dinner.

00:00:53.747 --> 00:00:54.673
Alright, news.

00:00:54.673 --> 00:00:55.863
Mostly last night.

00:00:55.863 --> 00:00:59.499
Democrats won control of both the House and the Senate.

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:10.804
That flips Congress away from Republicans for the back half of Trump's term, and it means a lot of what the White House wants now has to get through a Democratic majority.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:15.762
It also puts Brooklyn's own Hakeem Jeffries in line to be the next speaker.

00:01:15.762 --> 00:01:23.893
Closer to home, Hochul won a second term, beating Bruce Blakeman by more than twenty points with most of the votes counted.

00:01:23.893 --> 00:01:27.662
That's a lot wider than her six-point win four years ago.

00:01:27.662 --> 00:01:30.901
And all five city ballot proposals passed easily.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:33.810
The one that touches your ride is the third.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:43.263
It speeds up approvals for street safety projects like bike lanes and bus lanes, so fewer of them should get stuck in months of back and forth.

00:01:43.263 --> 00:01:51.263
Another one sets up a single permit office for a bunch of city agencies, though that won't open until twenty twenty-nine.

00:01:51.263 --> 00:01:53.246
And one from the design world.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:59.196
Canva is cutting or reshuffling about twelve hundred jobs, roughly a fifth of the company.

00:01:59.196 --> 00:01:59.857
The C.E.O.

00:01:59.857 --> 00:02:07.460
told staff it's the hardest moment in the company's history, and said growth slowed for the first time in a decade.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.443
It's part of a bigger squeeze.

00:02:09.443 --> 00:02:09.707
A.I.

00:02:09.707 --> 00:02:18.236
tools can now spit out the quick graphics people used to make in apps like that, and investors are cooling on the whole category.

00:02:18.236 --> 00:02:20.483
Today's challenge is a making one.

00:02:20.483 --> 00:02:24.979
At lunch, make a little bounce card out of one sheet of white paper.

00:02:24.979 --> 00:02:28.152
Fold it so it stands up on its own, like a tent.

00:02:28.152 --> 00:02:35.358
Then take one phone photo of your food or your coffee, with the window on one side and the card on the other.

00:02:35.358 --> 00:02:40.316
Move the card closer and farther until the shadows soften the way you like.

00:02:40.316 --> 00:02:43.093
It's the cheapest light modifier there is.

00:02:43.093 --> 00:02:46.597
Okay, something new today, and it's one for the bike.

00:02:46.597 --> 00:02:49.704
Why more air in your tires isn't always faster.

00:02:49.704 --> 00:02:53.935
Most of the drag from a tire comes from the tire itself bending.

00:02:53.935 --> 00:03:00.876
Every time a bit of the tire rolls onto the ground, it squashes flat, then springs back as it rolls away.

00:03:00.876 --> 00:03:04.711
The rubber and the casing don't give all that energy back.

00:03:04.711 --> 00:03:07.553
Some of it turns into a little bit of heat.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.272
That's rolling resistance.

00:03:09.272 --> 00:03:12.512
So on a perfectly smooth floor, harder is faster.

00:03:12.512 --> 00:03:16.280
More air means less squash, which means less energy lost.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.511
That's where the old idea of pumping tires rock hard comes from.

00:03:20.511 --> 00:03:22.560
But city streets aren't smooth.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:27.585
Over cracks, patches, and little bumps, a rock-hard tire can't swallow them.

00:03:27.585 --> 00:03:31.684
So the whole bike and your body get lifted and jolted instead.

00:03:31.684 --> 00:03:36.576
Your muscles and joints soak up that shaking, and that energy is gone too.

00:03:36.576 --> 00:03:42.129
Past a certain pressure, those losses grow faster than the tire's own losses shrink.

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:46.889
So adding more air actually makes you slower, not just less comfortable.

00:03:46.889 --> 00:03:48.475
Width plays into it too.

00:03:48.475 --> 00:03:56.607
At the same pressure, a wider tire touches the ground with about the same amount of rubber, but in a shorter, fatter patch.

00:03:56.607 --> 00:04:03.945
A short patch means less of the tire bends with each turn, so it rolls just as well, and you can run it softer.

00:04:03.945 --> 00:04:05.664
The floor is a pinch flat.

00:04:05.664 --> 00:04:11.349
Go too soft, and a sharp edge like a pothole lip can squeeze the tube against the rim.

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:15.977
So the sweet spot is just enough air to avoid that, and not much more.

00:04:15.977 --> 00:04:21.530
For rough city riding, that's usually lower than the max number printed on the side.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:30.058
So: calendar says gym at seven, the lens return in the morning, Godinger till five, a call at five-thirty, and the show at eight.

00:04:30.058 --> 00:04:31.777
And make that bounce card.

00:04:31.777 --> 00:04:35.678
The answer: a tiny same-as-before reply, with no file sent.

00:04:35.678 --> 00:04:37.000
Enjoy the sun, Ziad.
